# Notification seen vs read

Two clocks. Do not collapse them.

| State | Field | User meaning | UI |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Unseen** | `deliveredAt == null` | Has not opened/seen the inbox since it arrived | **Numeric badge** (app icon, bell count, `undeliveredCount`) |
| **Unread** | `readAt == null` | Has not opened the item / marked it read | **Dot** when the numeric count is zero; **highlight** on the row |

Opening the notifications surface marks **seen** (`deliveredAt`). That clears the number; a tier-colored dot remains while `readAt == null` notifications exist. Row unread state comes from **read** (`readAt`).

Post previews can be marked read automatically while visible. Retain their unread highlight
for the current inbox visit even after that acknowledgement. Seed the highlight from actual
unread rows, never from the badge count or list position. Preserve it through refresh,
pagination, and filter changes; reset on leaving/re-entering or account changes. Explicit
"Mark all as read" clears it immediately. Keep server read state and badge updates live.

Clicking through (or mark-read) sets `readAt` and should also set `deliveredAt` if it was still null.

Never drive the numeric badge off `readAt`. Never drive the unread dot or row highlight off `deliveredAt`.

Board and Articles navigation show only unread dots, across the entire section. Account badges
prioritize their combined numeric total, then fall back to unread notification existence.
Opening one identity’s inbox does not acknowledge another identity. Activity badge colors
follow the active identity’s tier. The native iOS Home Screen badge remains numeric only.
